# Dark Pool Congress — נתוני אמת בלבד

Do NOT calculate portfolio values, share amounts, or expectancy from raw congress trade events.
Congress trades only contain amount ranges.
Always fetch current holdings from the bioguide holdings source using `bioguide_id`.
Use `PriceChange` and `ExcessReturn` from DB/Quiver for performance metrics.

## Source of truth (this repo)

- Trades: `dark_pool_congress_trades` — `amount_label` (range), `filed_at`, `transaction_date`, `price_change_pct`, `excess_return_pct`, `spy_change_pct`.
- Holdings: cache `dark_pool_uw_snapshots` / `quiver_congress_holdings` → `by_bioguide[BioGuideID]` fields `CurrentHolding`, `Allocation`, `Ticker`. Not a table named `congress_stock_holdings`.
- Follows: `dark_pool_followed_investors` (+ local AsyncStorage). COUNT only — no "$ copied".
- Avg Delay = mean days `filed_at − transaction_date`. Honest. Win Rate from round-trips / Expectancy = forbidden.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — invented shares from a STOCK Act range
const qty = midpoint(amount_label) / yahooPrice;

// ✅ GOOD — range as disclosed; performance from Quiver columns
formatDisclosedAmountRange(trade.amount_label);
trade.price_change_pct; // PriceChange
trade.excess_return_pct; // ExcessReturn vs S&P
```
